From 7b3b19f28b92de213c35978b5698087c0920a3de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: round the IMX586 VANA vote

PM8150L BOB exposes 32 mV voltage steps starting at 3.0 V, so the
OxygenOS 3.3 V camera vote is not exactly representable.  An exact
3.3 V regulator request therefore fails with -EINVAL before the sensor
sequence starts.

Keep 3.3 V as the minimum and permit the next hardware step, 3.32 V, as
the maximum.  The regulator core will select 3.32 V, which is the closest
supported value that satisfies the downstream minimum.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hotdog-cam-scan.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hotdog-cam-scan.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hotdog-cam-scan.c
index 74267036bc86..90d6d707d0a7 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hotdog-cam-scan.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hotdog-cam-scan.c
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@
 
 #define HOTDOG_CAM_SCAN_MCLK_RATE	24000000
 #define HOTDOG_IMX586_MCLK_RATE		19200000
-#define HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_UV		3300000
+#define HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_MIN_UV	3300000
+#define HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_MAX_UV	3320000
 #define HOTDOG_IMX586_VDIG_LOAD_UA	1100000
 
 /*
@@ -206,8 +207,8 @@ static int hotdog_cam_scan_imx586(struct i2c_client *client,
 	 * while probing the EEPROM shared by the rear sensor pair.  Preserve
 	 * that board-level prerequisite while exercising the IMX586 sequence.
 	 */
-	ret = regulator_set_voltage(vana, HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_UV,
-				    HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_UV);
+	ret = regulator_set_voltage(vana, HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_MIN_UV,
+				    HOTDOG_IMX586_VANA_MAX_UV);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "cannot set IMX586 VANA voltage: %d\n", ret);
 		goto power_down;
-- 
2.50.1
